{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1284624-liches","id":1284624,"title":"Liches?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-03T18:16:02-08:00","id":1284624,"title":"Liches?","content":"What are your thoughts on the liches that exist in the WoD?<br /> <br /> Confusingly the &quot;lichs&quot; working with the True Black Hand are not actually liches in the traditional sense of the term. The so called liches of the TBH are mages that have been embraced, and become vampires. However, the Itarajana of the TBH apparently included traditional liches. Both groups were probably wiped out when Shadowlands Enoch was destroyed.<br /> <br /> But Larth Fulumchva is an actual lich. So were the Idran, possibly some of the Itarajana, and the Cabiri if you squint.<br /> <br /> That said, how do you feel about any of them? Have you ever used any of them in a game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":".  Larth made me do it. 02-03-2019, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T18:49:16-08:00","id":1284626,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve never used them in a game. I did create a WoD online play by post game that included them as a faction. There are a few ways one could go about having them. A lick is supposed to be a wizard who becomes indead to preserve his life, a gateway to immortality. With magic as we see in in M:tA, this isn\u2019t really an effective method. Far better just to use Life to make yourself younger. I think we would need some magical system that wasn\u2019t Mage.<br /> <br /> In a weird way, Tremere and his inner circle could be look at like lichee, they were wizards who sought to become immortal through magic and did it by transforming themselves into the undead. <br /> <br /> Sorcerer style magic works better for the lich concert I think. Less open ended and in some ways more flavorful. Maybe use Necromancy, the vampire Discipline. Mechanically maybe the best way to represent them would be with Risen. Risen with magical powers. Mummy touches on the concept as well and real mummies have some major lice overlap, especially if a canopic jar holds the phylactery. WoD mummies are too much alive though. Maybe the lice could be tied to Egypt, but but a mummy as canon presents them.<br /> <br /> Lichee should be old and powerful, with a lot of magical knowledge and power at their disposal. This suggests that there would be younger necromancers who have yet to achieve this state. In man6 regards they should be treated as an elder vampire - very powerful, smart, with a number of servants, who are difficult to tackle head on but may not be completely in touch with the modern world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-03T20:15:39-08:00","id":1284642,"title":"","content":"There's a write up for doing it as a rote in Dead magic and its one of the dauntain types for changeling...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T00:55:45-08:00","id":1284673,"title":"","content":"As Lian points out there is a Lich rote in Dead Magic and while it does grant immortality it does so at an exorbinant cost, it does indeed let you keep your Awakened Magick while also making you into one of the Undead but rather unfortunately one of the costs of the ritual is that your Arete is frozen at the level it was when you complete the ritual.<br /> <br /> I have used a Lich in a crossover chronicle although that particular Lich was rather unique in that he had made the necessary sacrifices to become one for selfless reasons. He was made into a Lich to stand as an eternal guardian to a bound demon. Unfortunately for all the demon got loose and his power alone was not nearly enough to defeat it, but he did become an ally of the PC\u2019s. He managed to give vital intel that helped the PC\u2019s to find a way to destroy the demon.<br /> <br /> But sadly the Lich rote is something most PC\u2019s would avoid as at the power level you are able to cast it you will have multiple means to extend your life at your fingertips already and the rotes costs are manifold and the frozen Arete is often the dealbreaker even if the player would be ready to pay the other costs. Not to mention how the rote itself is forbidden by almost all traditions and as such rather difficult to find. But storywise it is quite a nice rote offering quite excellent RP opportunities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T18:19:38-08:00","id":1285755,"title":"","content":"Keeping your arete frozen is 1000x times better than what the Tremere did...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T09:04:50-08:00","id":1285921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1284624-liches?p=1285755#post1285755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keeping your arete frozen is 1000x times better than what the Tremere did...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> Granted, the WoD is full of kludge (an ill-assorted collection of parts assembled to fulfill a particular purpose) in terms of setting and story. The Tremere were created as vampires long before the development of mage, and thus the setting's version of liches. However, it is interesting to speculate in-game why House Tremere became vampires rather than pursue lichdom. It makes the jyhad manipulations run deeper.<br /> <br /> As an aside, the CoD the Tremere did try to become liches - and it went sideways on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T15:46:38-08:00","id":1286036,"title":"","content":"Reading Dead Magick, my take is that the ritual requires too much individual dedication to be mass-produced, especially when you're part of a clan of magician but supposed to stay somehow isolated for a whole year from someone else's magick. Tremere wanted immortality for the entire clan instead, so they went looking for a different road.<br /> <br /> They probably got some formulas from the lichdom scraps but developed them around the power of the vampires, that were already able to use their own form of sorcery and didn't suffer from permanent paradox. The result was still going to be a static thaumivore mage, but with a lot of magical effects already embedded in their form: quintessence harvesting only required to drink blood rather than develop the Prime sphere, healing was only a matter of spending the acquired blood directly without casting any matter/life effect, decay was automatically kept in check...<br /> <br /> Lichdom may be more suited for a powerful mage, proficient in many Spheres (in fact, that's actually what the ritual requires), but to immortalize a whole occult sept vampirism was way more efficient and easy to use. Of course, they expected to keep their avatars and magical powers even after the transformation, so in their mind this vampirism ritual was expected to be superior and more effective than the old Etruscan lichdom.<br /> <br /> We now know it was not the case, but still a decent attempt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T23:41:59-08:00","id":1286370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1284624-liches?p=1285921#post1285921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes.<br /> <br /> Granted, the WoD is full of kludge (an ill-assorted collection of parts assembled to fulfill a particular purpose) in terms of setting and story. The Tremere were created as vampires long before the development of mage, and thus the setting's version of liches. However, it is interesting to speculate in-game why House Tremere became vampires rather than pursue lichdom. It makes the jyhad manipulations run deeper.<br /> <br /> As an aside, the CoD the Tremere did try to become liches - and it went sideways on them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Becoming a Vampire Makes sense with Ars Magica rules because true immortality is beyond it. Similarly DA mage keeps some of these issues in the Hermetic paradigm, with life extension becoming more and more expensive as time went on. That later sphere magick allowed a greater understanding and sythesis of magical ideas is one thing I think people regularly forget.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T07:41:55-08:00","id":1286437,"title":"","content":"Saulot made them do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T16:49:27-08:00","id":1286575,"title":"","content":"Well, him and Kupala anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-11T01:20:18-08:00","id":1286640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1284624-liches?p=1286370#post1286370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becoming a Vampire Makes sense with Ars Magica rules because true immortality is beyond it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I almost forgot about their Ars Magica origin XD Yes, the Twilight makes impossible to achieve true immortality there, and that was the whole point behind it. In the WoD, the concept of Twilight is partly engulfed in the Paradox one: as you become a Lich, you'll get at least one permanent paradox point. For every century or so of existence you'll gain another one (iirc the immortality rotes), meaning that a thousand years make you virtually a paradox lightning rod and two thousands might end up projecting you straight out of the Earth.<br /> <br /> Vampires can live forever with less immortality issues, so there's that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T15:40:57-08:00","id":1293902,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m DND when I found out lichee can be made with a level 14 ranger I opened my eyes to other possibilities. <br /> <br /> From a certain point of view you can subject lichdom to various ways:<br /> 1. Mage who messes up and paradox smacks him. He will likely suffer and want to kill himself to start over. <br /> 2. Mage who does it on purpose through various spheres. But he will lack progeny that vampires can create. <br /> 3. A risen with magic as previously stated. <br /> 4. Mummy can technically work for what you want.<br /> 5. An outside entity (perhaps demon or angel) binds you to this plane and/or object for whatever purpose. As a result you simply cannot die. It\u2019s a new curse altogether equally as powerful as the curse of Caine. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d probably throw in a mummy if it were me. Though I recall their power scale being much higher then most other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T23:09:38-08:00","id":1293973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1284624-liches?p=1285921#post1285921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granted, the WoD is full of kludge (an ill-assorted collection of parts assembled to fulfill a particular purpose) in terms of setting and story. The Tremere were created as vampires long before the development of mage, and thus the setting's version of liches. However, it is interesting to speculate in-game why House Tremere became vampires rather than pursue lichdom. It makes the jyhad manipulations run deeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as stated previously, Lichdom rituals are crazy obscure and totes forbidden. Assuming Tremere knew of the ritual - not an unreasonable assumption, though not a sure bet either - they couldn't just go around to other Hermetic Chantries, asking for ways to become undead abominations. Only a high ranking member of House Tremere could even be trusted to do that kind of investigation without the quest being discovered.<br /> <br /> And all the high ranking members of House Tremere were pursuing their own individual plans. No one had time to go looking for Lichdom, even if they wanted to pursue it.<br /> <br /> Remember, the inner circle only went with Goratrix's plan because they were under the impression that drinking a concoction distilled from vampire blood would make them living immortals. Them turning into vampires was a <i>surprise</i>, at least for most of the council (Goratrix and Tremere may have known, but if so they didn't share those suspicions). So it's safe to assume that, for those members, undeath was a hard sell, to be avoided if at all possible.<br /> <br /> So regardless of what influence the Jyhad might have had on mages who weren't even a part of it yet (that we know of), the more likely reason for the Tremere not pursuing Lichdom is significantly more mundane. Contingent on personal expectations, priorities, and risk-assessment. Sometimes, people do things because they seemed like good ideas at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-04T23:18:28-08:00","id":1293975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1284624-liches?p=1286370#post1286370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Becoming a Vampire Makes sense with Ars Magica rules because true immortality is beyond it. Similarly DA mage keeps some of these issues in the Hermetic paradigm, with life extension becoming more and more expensive as time went on. That later sphere magick allowed a greater understanding and sythesis of magical ideas is one thing I think people regularly forget.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also worth pointing out that, in the background of MtAs, the Tremere DID have immortality methods. The problem was that either the calcification of Reality or a dearth of magical resources made their original elixirs ineffective like they used to be. House Tremere scrambled for new and novel solutions because their original ones stopped working (like many large magical works did at the time). The exponential cost and downsides to immortality using regular magick was a <i>new</i> problem.<br /> <br /> Even when Spheres were developed, it didn't really stop the accrual of permanent Paradox from being a thing. Modern &quot;immortals&quot; still had to hunker down in Sancta or Horizon Realms in order to dodge that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-13T04:49:43-07:00","id":1296375,"title":"","content":"M20 Book of Secrets - Immortal Merit for 7 points + Phylactery Flaw for 7 points. There ya go, classic D&amp;D Lich who's true death is only met when their Phylactery is destroyed. Available at character creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-14T21:06:46-07:00","id":1296896,"title":"","content":"Assuming a Storyteller would be down with such a min-maxed character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T01:22:09-07:00","id":1296934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1284624-liches?p=1296896#post1296896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming a Storyteller would be down with such a min-maxed character.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't call that Min/Max. It's a great storytelling instrument. It might not be appropriate for all chronicles but it's hardly a power gaming type thing. You're breaking even.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T07:06:34-07:00","id":1296969,"title":"","content":"While M20 Phylactery has no right being a 7 dots Defect with all the benefits it confeers (I get why it's a Defect, I just don't think M20 version it's that bad of a Defect), I agree that such combo isn't min/maxed <i>per se</i>.<br /> <br /> If you consider the versatility of Mages dealing with an Immortal/Phylactery &quot;Lich&quot; isn't that big of a deal once you knows it's a Lich.<br /> <br /> You're exchanging a way of dying for another, which can surprise unprepared enemies. And your body can still be disabled if it's burned to ash (very easy in Mage), which wouldn't be lethal for this char but would still be inconvinient. Arguably superior forms of immortality are reachable at higher Sphere levels (things like preparing a spell to trigger on your death become possible)...but since destroying the Phylactery it's a &quot;special doom&quot; for this character these will be harder to reach (you will need special measures to prevent *that*)<br /> <br /> It does defeat the assumption that mages are frail of body and thus easy to kill if you attack fast and they're unprepared, though. Such a character changes a few assumptions about mages, which it's alright in my book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-15-2019, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T09:08:34-07:00","id":1297005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PazuzuAxelf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1284624-liches?p=1296934#post1296934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't call that Min/Max.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could not think of a better term - and in any case, the character is immortal and nearly indestructible. Following the rules of being an Evil Overlord (you put the phylactery in a bank vault) and the PC becomes one of the most powerful characters in the part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T10:29:49-07:00","id":1297021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1284624-liches?p=1297005#post1297005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Following the rules of being an Evil Overlord (you put the phylactery in a bank vault) and the PC becomes one of the most powerful characters in the part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the character has to be touching the Phylactery to cast any spells, that would be...inconvinient.<br /> <br /> In particular if his body it's burnt or otherwise destroyed beyond regen. In that case all that remains of the Mage will be a very angry Phylactery trapped in a bank vault. Now that I think about it, that could fuel a story or two.<br /> <br /> Still it's true that it can be a powerful combo in a combat oriented game. I didn't suggested it fo an OP starting character thread for nothing...it's just that by itself it doesn't <i>have </i>to be OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T00:19:12-07:00","id":1297173,"title":"","content":"As Aleph says, putting your Phylactery in a bank vault severely limits your power. You have to keep it with you at all times in order to use Magick. <br /> <br /> Give <i>Book of Secrets</i> a read, it's quite good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T16:09:29-07:00","id":1303210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1284624-liches?p=1293973#post1293973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, the inner circle only went with Goratrix's plan because they were under the impression that drinking a concoction distilled from vampire blood would make them living immortals. Them turning into vampires was a <i>surprise</i>, at least for most of the council (Goratrix and Tremere may have known, but if so they didn't share those suspicions). So it's safe to assume that, for those members, undeath was a hard sell, to be avoided if at all possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tremere knew though. He says this himself in Blood Treachery. He went along with Goratrix's plan despite knowing. Perhaps he believed he would be able to step back but he makes abundantly clear between the risk of dying with magic (at the time Tremere was convinced Magic was dying while it was just changing) and immortality in a lesser form he choose the latter option.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-06T16:48:03-07:00","id":1303219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1284624-liches?p=1303210#post1303210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tremere knew though. He says this himself in Blood Treachery. He went along with Goratrix's plan despite knowing. Perhaps he believed he would be able to step back but he makes abundantly clear between the risk of dying with magic (at the time Tremere was convinced Magic was dying while it was just changing) and immortality in a lesser form he choose the latter option.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that may be true (I couldn't be bothered to read the &quot;play&quot; part of Blood Treachery, just the crunch at the end). But my point was that, regardless of what Tremere and Goratrix wanted, the other members of the council were firmly under the impression that Goratrix's elixir would give them immortality, not vampirism. They probably would not have accepted the plan had Goratrix been forthcoming about the risks to their lives/souls/Avatars.<br /> <br /> Moreover, House Tremere was not lacking in ideas for how to prolong their lives. If given the choice between becoming vampires and taking a shot at their individual plans, there's no contest. They went along with Goratrix's plan because he seemed so sure it would work. And Tremere himself seemed confident in the plan, so to them it seemed &quot;worth a try&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T08:32:10-07:00","id":1303324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1284624-liches?p=1303219#post1303219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that may be true (I couldn't be bothered to read the &quot;play&quot; part of Blood Treachery, just the crunch at the end). But my point was that, regardless of what Tremere and Goratrix wanted, the other members of the council were firmly under the impression that Goratrix's elixir would give them immortality, not vampirism. They probably would not have accepted the plan had Goratrix been forthcoming about the risks to their lives/souls/Avatars.<br /> <br /> Moreover, House Tremere was not lacking in ideas for how to prolong their lives. If given the choice between becoming vampires and taking a shot at their individual plans, there's no contest. They went along with Goratrix's plan because he seemed so sure it would work. And Tremere himself seemed confident in the plan, so to them it seemed &quot;worth a try&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>They went along with Goratric (Etrius included, and Etrius hated Goratrix) because Tremere said so. And you are right, they did not know the effect of the potion, even Goratrix did not, as he was convinced he had found a way to solve the problem and enjoyed the praise of his master. Tremere on the other hand knew but he made the choice anyway<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blood Treachery</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have lived... No. I have existed for over a thousand years, and that is a great deal of time to ponder one's actions. Most of all, I dwell upon the fortunes that brought me to this. If I had any cause left to believe that Hell had power over me, I might fear for my decrepit soul. More than anyone else, I can appreciate the chains of the flesh and the yearning to escape upward.<br /> I knew full well what would happen when I drank that potion, brewed from the blood of a monster. I knew even then that I sentenced my Daemon to death, that I would lose my magic and be forever outcast from the light of day. Oh yes, I knew the consequences of my actions. However, I knew the mysteries of Fate also, child. The secrets of the Ars Fati were no less compelling in my day than in yours. When the vis began to die, I, like many others, looked to the mysteries contained in unraveling threads. What we discovered, all of us, pleased no one. The cowardly retreated from the world. The proud denied the truth until it ground them underfoot. The brave perished, raging against the turning of Fortune's Wheel. The resourceful? You look now upon the last of them.<br /> I have outlived many enemies. I have deceived Death. I have cheated even the fall of magic. I have usurped the legacy of the First Murderer and supped on souls until my own empty heart grew heavy with the echoes of their anguish. Who, or what, speaks through you, child, that I who may yet see the unmaking of Time, hear in your words that distant stirring of the mystic sight I and my kind murdered a millennium ago?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-07T15:52:31-07:00","id":1303423,"title":"","content":"That passage is pretty good - even if the final question is so tangled I'm not certain what he was asking. That said, I wonder how things stand with Tremere the wizard now in V5, with its retcons of the timeline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-08T05:13:24-07:00","id":1303500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1284624-liches?p=1303423#post1303423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That passage is pretty good - even if the final question is so tangled I'm not certain what he was asking</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it just happens that when Tremere (Saulot?, Tremere in Goroatrix body?) was about to blast the Hermetic leadership to put an end to the 2nd Massa War, a young mage that wanted peace got possessed by the Oracle of Entropy, whom proceded to utter a criptic prophesy to the elder about how war it's bad and destroying the OoH would end his own ambitions because their fates are linked or some bullshit like that.<br /> <br /> My interpretation of the whole &quot;who or what speaks through you that I, of all people, feel that it would be better to heed your words and not kill everyone like I was about to do&quot; it's that Tremere understood that this prophesy was no joking matter, and (correctly) attributed it to more than the fast-cast of an apprentice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">That said, I wonder how things stand with Tremere the wizard now in V5, with its retcons of the timeline.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Yeah, right. He wasn't reported dead, so we should assume he's still out there. With the Tremere clan divided it's the perfect time to recover rulership of</span><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> his clan, too, it wouldn't be surprising if he's behind a House or two.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-08-2019, 08:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T12:39:37-07:00","id":1304008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1284624-liches?p=1303423#post1303423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That passage is pretty good - even if the final question is so tangled I'm not certain what he was asking. That said, I wonder how things stand with Tremere the wizard now in V5, with its retcons of the timeline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nitpick: You're using retcon incorrectly. Nothing about the timeline was retroactively changed. They didn't go back and decide that &quot;oh this didn't happen&quot; or anything like that. The continuity has continued.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-10T19:17:55-07:00","id":1304070,"title":"","content":"Hairsplitting: A change in continuity like that would create retcons. Because if it is not Tremere delivering that speech, then who is delivering it? Or was it delivered at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-12T06:07:46-07:00","id":1304435,"title":"","content":"Again, nothing has been changed in the continuity. Everything pointing to Saulot being in control of Tremere's body is pre-V20. V5 didn't create this issue, Revised did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-14T15:57:09-07:00","id":1304901,"title":"","content":"It's pretty clear that's Tremere talking. Saulot would not have bothered or have reason to go there searching for what was left of the Order of Hermes. The way he talks (Vis instead of quintessence, or daemon instead of avatar for example) is meant to represent a medieval mage and it reminds of Ars Magica terminology. <br /> And there's no reason the one speaking could not be Tremere in Goratrix's body. Keep in mind revisited suggested Tremere killed the antitribu to lower his generation to third again, so he would have had the power to deal with a bunch of masters and adepts (but not the Oracle manifesting itself in the middle of the scene).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}